1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,280
Every airplane window has a tiny hole in it.

2
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:05,240
You've probably sat right next to one

3
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:06,430
and never noticed.

4
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:07,570
It's not a crack,

5
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:09,280
and it's not a defect.

6
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:10,900
It's there on purpose,

7
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,170
and it quietly does two jobs.

8
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:15,240
Most people assume a plane window

9
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:16,690
is one thick sheet.

10
00:00:16,830 --> 00:00:18,260
It's actually three.

11
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:19,520
The pane you can touch

12
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:21,130
is just a scratch shield.

13
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,020
It holds back no pressure at all.

14
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:26,220
Behind it sit two strong acrylic panes:

15
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:28,340
a middle one and an outer one.

16
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:29,660
At cruising altitude,

17
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,600
the air outside is thin.

18
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:34,170
The air inside is kept much denser,

19
00:00:34,190 --> 00:00:36,670
so it pushes outward on every window

20
00:00:36,690 --> 00:00:38,860
with hundreds of kilos of force.

21
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:40,020
That tiny hole

22
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,720
goes through the middle pane.

23
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:44,240
Cabin air flows into the gap behind it,

24
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:45,530
so the middle pane feels

25
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:47,580
equal pressure on both sides.

26
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,740
The outer pane carries the whole load,

27
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,360
and the middle pane waits,

28
00:00:51,420 --> 00:00:53,170
unstressed, as a backup.

29
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:54,560
Job number two:

30
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:57,310
that same airflow lets moisture escape,

31
00:00:57,330 --> 00:01:00,310
so the gap stays clear of fog and frost.

32
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:01,910
One tiny hole.

33
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:04,180
A spare window and a defogger.

34
00:01:04,260 --> 00:01:05,300
What everyday thing

35
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:06,800
should we unpack next?
